# Docker build context (P2-M7.3, D-M7.3-4 / P0-a).
#
# Once image digests are contractual, an uncontrolled build context is two
# problems at once: a leak path for operator secrets, and a source of
# nondeterminism that would be misattributed to the release process. Every
# Dockerfile here does `COPY . .`, so this file is the only thing standing
# between a developer's working tree and the bytes we sign.
#
# Docker does NOT support brace expansion. Patterns are matched against the
# path relative to the context root, so a nested match needs its own `**/`
# form; both are listed where nesting is possible.
#
# Verified by scripts/check-build-context.sh, which probes a real build rather
# than modelling these semantics.

# --- Version control and CI ------------------------------------------------
# .git is never enumerated by `git ls-files`, which is why the gate is a probe
# build. Excluding it also keeps the context stable across branches.
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Operator secrets and per-deployment material --------------------------
docker/.env
docker/.env.*
docker/docker-compose.override.yml
deploy/operator/invites
deploy/operator/import
nova-config
nova-secrets
nova-postgres-data
nova-kubo-data
nova-tmp-uploads
*.key
**/*.key
*.pem
**/*.pem

# --- Local build outputs ---------------------------------------------------
# The context must not vary with whatever a developer last built. node_modules
# is also a correctness fix: coordinator.Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then
# `COPY . .`, so a host node_modules would overwrite the installed one.
bin
dist
build
/coordinator
/novactl
/node
/setup-wizard
coverage.out
coverage.html
node_modules
**/node_modules
web/admin/dist
web/widget/dist
web/setup/dist

# --- Not part of any image -------------------------------------------------
reports
simulations
docs/nova-upstream-findings.md
.claude
.superpowers
.editorconfig
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
**/*.swp

# web/ itself stays: the coordinator image builds the three SPA bundles.
